                                "sense_id": "ebd15448-f0a8-3215-b139-723be944a711",
                                "text": "Analarin, a priest, spoke of boxwood rattles, which were used to announce the clergy from the ninth century. The crécelle, or 'cressel', was once used in Roman Catholic churches during Passion Week instead of a bell."
                            }
                        ]
